# Hodge Theory without Varieties over ℤ

Umbrella for the arithmetic Kähler package of the divisibility–successor complex: Kähler packages
and the transport of Hodge–Riemann along connected families; stars as lower horizons, the boundary
flux and the self-similar counterterm that selects `Λ`; stars of the complete Weil family and local
Hodge–Riemann on deep stars; the Liouville property; the nerve of the star cover; the links of the
dilation complex; the depth law of stars; the Künneth step for spectral gaps; the three Lefschetz
candidates; the Möbius gluing of the stars, the recursion of the renormalized prime form over
the nerve, the gcd stratification of the complete Weil family, the shell balance law on the
coherent sector, the layers of a prime (the Künneth step at the horizon), the sign gauge on
deep stars, the Möbius duality between conductors and stars, its lcm grading, and the
cross-conductor pairings; and the homotopy equivalence between the squarefree prime complex
and its wedge of spheres indexed by odd squarefree integers in the upper half-window.
See `HodgeTheoryWithoutVarieties/README.md`.
